    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Cardboard boxes. Broken glass. Old doors. Painted "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "handrails",
            "zh": "栏杆"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This is American artist Redic’s home in Shanghai. You might think he is living in a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "rubbish dump",
            "zh": "垃圾场"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But Redic calls his house a "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "gallery"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The artist has lived in Shanghai for 13 years. He likes to walk around the city and collect “rubbish”. Later, he will turn these “useless” items into artworks."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Redic started to create art with "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "recycled",
            "ref": "v-recycled"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " materials when he was in college. He first came to China to visit the 2010 Shanghai Expo. After staying in the city for several days, however, he decided that he didn’t want to leave. He had fallen in love with Shanghai."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, Redic is always happy to give people a tour of his “gallery”. He explains the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "back stories",
            "zh": "幕后故事"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of each piece of work. Take “Doors of Life” for example. Redic collected the doors from different "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "corners",
            "ref": "v-corner"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of Shanghai. He covered them in his own modern art. While creating these artworks, the artist often came up with some "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "poetry lines",
            "zh": "诗句"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". And he painted them on the doors. Redic has always been interested in doors. He says doors deliver “important messages” like “as one door closes, another opens”."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "This year, Redic is "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "heading off to",
            "ref": "v-head-off-to"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Europe with some of his works. The artist wants to share his experiences in Shanghai with the world."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The next time you want to throw something away, give it a second look. As Redic has said, we should always “leave the door open”."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
